Subject: Urgent – Adverse Event Report: Metformin 1000mg Batch MF-2024-0089

Dear Pharmacovigilance Team,

I am writing to report a serious adverse event potentially linked to
Metformin Hydrochloride Extended-Release Tablets 1000 mg supplied by your
company.

On 18 April 2024, three patients at City Hospital, Mumbai were admitted
with severe gastrointestinal distress (persistent vomiting, abdominal pain,
and elevated lactate levels) within 6 hours of taking their regular
Metformin dose. All three patients were on a stable, long-term Metformin
regimen with no prior adverse reactions.

The tablets dispensed were from Batch No. MF-2024-0089, manufactured in
February 2024 and due to expire in January 2026. The quantity involved
across the three patients was approximately 90 tablets.

Patient details have been anonymised per regulatory guidelines but are
available on request under a data-sharing agreement.

Product Details:
  Product    : Metformin Hydrochloride Extended-Release Tablets
  Strength   : 1000 mg
  Batch No.  : MF-2024-0089
  Mfg. Date  : 10 February 2024
  Expiry     : 09 January 2026
  Qty        : ~90 tablets (3 patients x 30 tablets/month pack)
  Source     : Distributed via City Hospital central pharmacy

This report is being submitted simultaneously to the Central Drugs Standard
Control Organisation (CDSCO) as per Schedule Y requirements.

We request immediate investigation, batch recall consideration, and a CAPA
response within 72 hours given the critical patient safety implications.

Yours sincerely,
Dr. Priya Nair, MD
Clinical Pharmacology, City Hospital Mumbai
